Hi everyone. I've been playing Nethack on and off for about a year and
so far the farthest I have gotten has been to make it down to the
lowest level with all three items. Killed by a touch of death. =(

I've read all the spoilers I could get my hands on time and time again,
but I have a few questions that I don't really think are covered in
them. If anyone could spend a few minutes letting me in on some of your
knowledge it would be much appreciated.

1. How do people continuously polymorph pets? It seems to me that once
they step on a polymorph trap, if they step on it again nothing will
happen and I'm often left with a useless pet.

2. How do people get so many hit points? The most I ever had was 350
and it was the result of thousands of turns of potion collection and
reverse nurse genociding. When I read YAAPs it seems standard to have
over 400 and in some cases over 600.

3. I find pets to be unbearably annoying. Whenever I've tried to use
the pet as a bodyguard they end up running all over the place while I'm
desperately running in circles around them trying to get them to attack
whatever is chasing me until I die. How do other players use pets
effectively?

4. Is Touch of Death a spell? My most promising character was killed by
the Wizard of Yendor by a touch of death, and I had an AC of -52 and
magic resistance, magic cancellation, and pretty much every other
intrinsic you could imagine (not disentegration though, I was a
vegetarian). What could I have done to avoid death in this situation,
aside from wear an amulet of life saving? (come to think of it, I bet
that it is a spell and that he stole my quest artifact and took my only
magic resistance, but I'll leave this up just in case)

5. Is there anything more annoying than a tough enemy with a wand of
digging? My last game Baalzebub had a wand of digging and I spent an
amazing amount of turns hunting him down and accidentally falling
through the holes... luckily Demogorgon didn't pop as a result of this,
but sheesh, probably one of the most aggravating Nethack experiences to
date. What would you guys do in this situation?

6. How do you re-assign an objects key? For example if I want to
eliminate confusion between lowercase "L" and uppercase "I" by naming
those two keys to something like my main armor and helmet. I've read
through the help file for commands a few times and I don't see it
mentioned anywhere, but I think I've seen it mentioned on r.g.r.n.

7. I play in tiles mode. When you step on a pile of items that is
between 2 and 5 items I believe it brings up an annoying pop-up on the
side displaying the contents of the pile instead of saying "there are
many items here." Is there any simple way to change it so that it never
displays this pop-up?

8. How can I set my game so that the same options are enabled every
time I begin a new game? I use the tiled windows version of 3.4.3 and
every game I begin I always turn autopickup off, showexp on and autodig
on. It's a minor annoyance, but I'd like to fix it.

Thanks to anyone who reads this. Happy hacking everyone.



